From 13a5c98ec60c78f914639583b2775fc5fcc4c39a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Circelli <ryancircelli@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:09:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat(ipc/server): deferred requests and blocking waits

A handler can set ServerContext::defer to hold its request unanswered;
the manager saves the message and pointer buffer, keeps serving other
sessions, and re-dispatches the request (ServerContext::resumed) when
the deferral's handle signals or its deadline passes. This lets one
server thread serve blocking calls (async forwards, socket waits)
without stalling every other session.

Also:
- the manager waits with no timeout when nothing is deferred, instead
  of waking every 100us;
- prepare_wait_handles never writes past MAX_OBJECT_COUNT;
- ISessionObject::on_session_closed (default no-op) tells the object
  which session closed, so per-session state can be dropped.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Circelli <ryancircelli@gmail.com>
